# Keep the eval harness out of the corpus it measures.
#
# klams-mind sprint 007. `evals/suites/*.toml` is text engineered to
# lexically match every query it contains, so once the scanner indexes
# it, it wins those queries outright — the suite starts measuring
# itself. Observed 2026-07-26: the suite surfaced at rank 0-1 for
# several queries, and a `no_hallucination` check failed because its own
# forbidden term ("Duke Courses") was found *in the suite file*.
#
# `evals/baselines/*.md` is worse: it is generated output carrying every
# query plus the paths that answered it, so each refreshed baseline
# contaminates the next run a little more.
#
# klams's scanner honours a repo-root .klamsignore (klams-scanner
# walk.rs) and prunes chunks for files it no longer walks, so this
# self-heals on the next scan cycle.
evals/
